# BulkDownloader fleet -- one "label address" per line.
#
# COPY THIS to ~/.config/bd/hosts and put YOUR addresses in it. This example is
# tracked and therefore public, so the addresses below are RFC 5737
# documentation addresses and are deliberately not real ones.
#
# The label is matched against `hostname`: a line whose label is this machine
# deploys LOCALLY instead of over ssh, so the same file works from any host in
# the fleet without a special case for "me".
#
# THAT INFERENCE IS scripts/deploy_fleet.sh's, AND bd-fleet-run DOES NOT SHARE
# IT (v3.66.1142). A fleet label is not a hostname -- CLAUDE.md's front matter
# records bd-jobs refusing a real host because a LABEL had no DNS entry -- so
# deciding "run here or over there" from a name match is wrong in both
# directions. bd-fleet-run reads locality from an explicit OPTIONAL THIRD
# COLUMN instead:
#
#     master   192.0.2.10   local
#
# Any other value, or no third column, means remote. The column is ignored by
# `bd-fleet` (read_hosts takes parts[0]/parts[1]) and by deploy_fleet.sh (which
# reads `label addr _rest`), so adding it is backward compatible with both.
#
# scripts/deploy_fleet.sh refuses (exit 2) if this file is missing or lists no
# hosts -- an empty fleet must never read as a successful deploy of nothing.

master   192.0.2.10
candidate 192.0.2.11
clean    192.0.2.12
